# Build artefacts
/target/
**/target/

# Cargo lockfile policy:
#   For *binaries* / *firmware* the lockfile SHOULD be committed so builds
#   are reproducible bit-for-bit. ezal-firmware is the binary here, so we
#   keep Cargo.lock under version control. (It lives at the workspace root.)
# (No ignore entry for Cargo.lock — committed deliberately.)

# Editor backups and swap files
**/*.rs.bk
*.swp
.idea/
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
!.vscode/settings.json

# Nix / direnv
# `.envrc` is committed (it just says `use flake`); the local cache that
# direnv writes alongside it is not, and neither are `nix build` outputs.
.direnv/
result
result-*

# Secrets: WiFi credentials for STA mode live in .env, which build.rs bakes
# into the firmware at compile time. Never commit it — the committed template
# is .env.example. (`.env.example` is re-included so it stays tracked.)
.env
!.env.example

# AI tooling
.antigravitycli/

# OS junk
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# probe-rs / cargo-flash artefacts
*.uf2
*.bin
*.hex
# …but the vendored CYW43439 radio firmware blobs ARE tracked — they're a
# build input (`include_bytes!`d into the image), not a build artefact. See
# crates/ezal-firmware/cyw43-firmware/README.md for their provenance.
!crates/ezal-firmware/cyw43-firmware/*.bin

# defmt log dumps
*.defmt
